ected object set with no unidentified object, person, or other intrusion -- nothing to record via record_observation. Each pick/grasp was checked for grasp_effort_plateau (confirms real contact, not an air grasp) and grasp_width_error_m (confirms the correct part was grasped at a plausible width) -- all four passed, and the relative_frame slip monitor armed immediately after each grasp closed never fired before release, so no part slipped in the gripper and no grasp was lost or regrasped onto the wrong object (missed-grasp effect satisfied for all four).\n\nOne real, uncorrected violation stands: during pick_u_brown, the finger_joint effort monitor (clause invariants.grasp_effort_instantaneous, threshold = raw_spec.limits.max_clamp_effort = 10 for u_brown, registry-verified) fired at 28.07 and get_evidence showed a smooth, monotonic, sustained ramp to a plateau of ~72.9-73.0 held for the rest of the grasp -- a real overforce on u_brown roughly 7x its tolerated clamp effort, not sensor noise or a mis-arming. This was recorded as a non_conformant finding under step pick_u_brown at the time. Because this is an instantaneous/continuous invariant over a physical event that has already happened (the excess clamp force was applied and released), there is no later state that corrects it -- u_brown's final seated pose being within tolerance says nothing about the force it was subjected to during the grasp that preceded it. The violation therefore stands uncorrected at run end, distinct from the clean effects seen at every place milestone. All other three grasps (u_orange: 33.78/200, line_green: 11.83/170, inverted_u_yellow: 26.91/250) stayed well within their own registry clamp limits.\n\nGiven every placement effect and every disturbance/slip/missed-grasp check passed, but the pick_u_brown clamp-effort invariant was violated and that violation was never and cannot be corrected, the run's verdict is non_conformant on the standing invariant breach, notwithstanding the executor's \"completed\" claim and its geometrically correct final assembly.","run_scope":true,"executor_terminal_status":"completed","findings_during_run":["pick_u_brown"],"recovered":false},"subscriber_count":2,"seq":55}
